WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.934
-Donald Trump kicked off
his 2024 presidential bid

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:06.601
with a series of campaign
stops in key primary states

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:09.834
and attacks on his main rival,
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis.

00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:12.667
And yet, even as Trump forges
ahead with a 2024 bid

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:15.634
that no one except his hardcore
fans seems to want,

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:17.567
everyone who actually
has the power to stop him,

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:18.901
whether it's his
fellow Republicans

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.901
or federal prosecutors,
has refused to take action,

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:24.968
hoping he'll magically go away,
just like they did in 2016.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:27.434
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:29.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:33.634
The Republican Party is facing
a reckoning right now

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:36.067
over its future after
its disastrous performances

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:37.501
in three straight
national elections,

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:40.334
which have left the party
weak, fractured and rudderless.

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:42.133
And who better to help
with that reckoning

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:43.801
than MyPillow CEO
Mike Lindell.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.701
The Republican
National Committee

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.167
pledged to work
with Lindell

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:48.868
and keep him involved
in the party's leadership

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:52.100
after Lindell ran to become
the chair of the RNC.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.100
Sadly, Lindell lost
that election on Friday

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.934
to current chair Ronna McDaniel.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:58.701
Or so they say.

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:01.767
And I hope I don't sound
too much like Mike Lindell

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:03.334
when I say this,
but I think he

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:05.834
only lost because China,
Hugo Chavez,

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:09.100
the CIA and Dominion teamed up
to steal the election from him!

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.701
And also she may be ahead now,

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:13.033
but sometimes slow
and steady wins the race!

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:16.467
Like in that story,
the tortoise and the hare!

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:19.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:22.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:26.334
I think -- I think in the end,
I did sound a little like him.

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:27.501
Anyway, Lindell lost,

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:29.634
but he made it clear
that he's still expected

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.868
to be closely involved
with the GOP leadership

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.300
after a poll
of Republican voters

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.133
showed he was their favorite
to take over the RNC.

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:38.734
-We need to hold
the RNC accountable.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:41.033
They did say,
"I will work with Mike Lindell.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.167
I can't wait to work
with Mike Lindell."

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:47.234
And Ronna said she would work,
she would do a grassroots tour

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:49.133
But she also said,
I'm looking forward

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:50.601
to working with Mike Lindell.

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.033
Steve, what do you work --

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.033
what do you think I've been
working on for two years?

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:56.133
So this is a wake up
call to them.

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.601
You better wake up.
I better get that phone call.

00:01:58.601 --> 00:01:59.968
-Okay, word of advice, Mike.

00:01:59.968 --> 00:02:01.834
You need to be a little quieter

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:04.334
or else you're not going to hear
when that phone rings.

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:06.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.734
I mean, just watch
all these missed calls.

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:09.434
-Let's look into it.
[ Telephone ringing ]

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:12.267
What are they hiding, Steve?
What are they hiding?

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:13.767
They're running out of track...
[ Telephone ringing ]

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:16.100
...where they're not going to be
able to keep going these dumps

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.767
or it's going to be too obvious.

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.601
Open it up
and look good in there.

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:20.701
They're all the computers.
[ Telephone ringing ]

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.734
They go horizontal, everybody.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.734
-And just to show that she was
serious about keeping Lindell

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.400
involved at the highest levels
of the GOP,

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.501
McDaniel made a show of
inviting him on stage,

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:31.067
along with one other
fellow candidate,

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:32.367
former Trump campaign lawyer

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:34.200
Harmeet Dhillon
after McDaniel won,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.434
even calling Lindell
a leader in the GOP.

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:38.234
-Thank you.
We got to --

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:40.167
we got to get Mike
and Harmeet up here.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:41.901
Mike and Harmeet,
can you please come up?

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:43.667
Thank you
for the race you ran,

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:45.834
for the leaders
you are in our party.

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:48.434
We are so grateful for you.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:51.033
We need all of us.
We heard you, grassroots.

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:54.167
We know. We heard Harmeet.
We heard Mike Lindell.

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:57.033
But with us united
and all of us going together,

00:02:57.033 --> 00:03:00.834
the Democrats
are going to hear us in 2024

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:03.200
when we take back the
White House and the Senate.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.267
-I mean, that's a dream team
right there.

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:07.968
Ronna McDaniel,
who oversaw three straight

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:10.534
blowout losses in '18, '20
and '22,

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:13.334
Harmeet Dhillon, legal advisor
for Donald Trump's 2020 campaign

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:16.300
and a pillow salesman famous
for getting his phone seized

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.167
by the FBI at a Hardee's
drive-through, a real thing.

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:20.367
A real thing that happened.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:21.801
This is a very real headline.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.400
In fact, the feds
disguise themselves

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.767
as the drive-through menu

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:27.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:30.667
It was so weird for everyone who
drove through before Lindell.

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:33.133
"Hey, are you dude dressed up
like a sign?"

00:03:33.133 --> 00:03:34.567
"Keep driving."

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:36.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:38.667
No one expects to lose a phone
at a drive-through.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:41.167
There's no video of it,
but we do have audio

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.901
of Lindell's order
after the seizure.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.534
Should I tell them?

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:56.567
That was me, you guys.

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:58.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.834
I did both voices.

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:02.868
Now, in case you forgot
the specifics of this story,

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.834
Lindell had his phone seized
as part of an FBI investigation

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:07.734
into a Republican county clerk
in Colorado

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.033
who tampered
with voting equipment

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:10.767
to investigate
nonexistent voter fraud.

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:13.968
And despite that,
Trump is still his friend,

00:04:13.968 --> 00:04:15.567
and the chair
of the Republican Party

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:17.567
says he should be involved
in the party's leadership.

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:20.167
I honestly can't think of any
Democratic equivalent to this.

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:22.534
Like, imagine if Joe Biden
brought a guy on stage

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:25.400
who sells compression socks
and claims the moon is actually

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.367
just a projection
to distract people.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.234
"Alright, everybody,
I'd like to introduce

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:31.300
MySock CEO, Rick Kordell.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.033
Great guy, great patriot
who makes great socks

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:34.567
and he says the moon isn't
real."

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:38.400
"But we got room
for a lot of ideas

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.667
inside the Democratic Party.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:41.334
What's that? What's that, Rick?
Now, okay.

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:42.868
He's telling me Google Maps
is an invention

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:46.200
of lizard people,
and these lizard people

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.901
are using it
to coordinate an attack.

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:49.767
That's great stuff, Rick.

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:51.167
That's why I don't use maps.

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.067
I just wander around until
someone tells me where to go."

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:55.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:59.801
So that's the position
the GOP finds itself in.

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.734
They all want to pretend
that Trump and his gang

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.634
and weirdos are done,
but they also don't think

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:04.934
they have a future without them.

00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:06.601
For example, on the one hand,
they keep insisting

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:09.033
over and over that
Trump is the past

00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:11.000
and that he can't win
a general election.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.667
-Donald Trump kept saying,

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:13.868
we're going to be
winning so much,

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:15.367
we'll get tired of winning.

00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:17.167
I'm tired of losing.
I mean, it's all he's done.

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:18.734
-Look, I don't think he can
win in '20 --

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:20.334
in November of '24.

00:05:20.334 --> 00:05:21.834
-Trump is the past.

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:24.067
He's fading fast.
He's a proven loser.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.601
He cost us the House at '18.

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:26.901
He cost us
the White House in '20.

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:29.334
He cost us the Senate
again and again.

00:05:29.334 --> 00:05:30.701
And I think we all know that,

00:05:30.701 --> 00:05:31.968
and I think we're moving
past Trump.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.100
-Does Trump win?

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.334
I hope so.
I love the guy.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:37.234
And a week ago,
I would have said slam dunk.

00:05:37.234 --> 00:05:40.300
But after how last night
shook out, I don't know now.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.133
-I've said over and over again

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:44.234
that he can't
win a general election.

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:45.934
And that's not speculation.

00:05:45.934 --> 00:05:47.734
That's based upon the polling

00:05:47.734 --> 00:05:51.734
that I was privy
to pre the 2020 election

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:54.834
and what we saw actually happen
in the 2020 election.

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:56.434
And it's only gotten worse
since then.

00:05:56.434 --> 00:05:59.534
Then add to it
what you saw happen in 2022,

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:02.534
and I think Republicans
are recognizing that.

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:04.734
-Sure, Chris Christie,
you maybe said it over and over,

00:06:04.734 --> 00:06:07.334
but that was after you said over
and over he should be president

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:08.567
and he should be reelected.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.200
You were one of the first
elected Republicans

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.601
to support him in 2016.

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:13.934
You helped him prep
for his debates in 2020.

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:17.067
You even stood behind him
at press conferences in 2016

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:20.400
like a presenter
at the Golden Globes

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.234
who had just handed him
an award

00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:25.133
and forgot to get out
of the shot.

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:27.601
[ Whispering ] "Chris, get off
stage!

00:06:27.601 --> 00:06:29.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:32.300
Chris!

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:36.801
Get off...

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:39.334
Get off stage!"

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:41.133
[ Normal voice] In fact, the
parallels between how the GOP

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.133
is treating Trump now
and how they treated him

00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:44.667
in 2016 are pretty alarming.

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:47.267
You might remember the exact
same thing happening back then.

00:06:47.267 --> 00:06:49.467
Republicans kept insisting
there was no way

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:51.701
Trump could get enough support
to win the primary,

00:06:51.701 --> 00:06:53.901
that he had a hard ceiling
that he would lose

00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:56.200
once the party
coalesced around an alternative

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.000
and that he would definitely get
crushed in a general election.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.000
-What you're seeing is a sense
that the party is not going

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.601
to coalesce around Donald Trump
if he is the nominee.

00:07:04.601 --> 00:07:07.767
-If the Republican Party
becomes the party of David Duke,

00:07:07.767 --> 00:07:09.334
Donald Trump, I'm out.

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:11.000
-Senate Majority Leader
Mitch McConnell

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:15.934
told GOP colleagues they can
drop Trump "like a hot rock."

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:17.667
-He's got a high floor
and a low ceiling,

00:07:17.667 --> 00:07:19.167
in my opinion.
I mean, Donald Trump

00:07:19.167 --> 00:07:22.567
has proven himself
capable of getting 25% to 30%.

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:25.968
-Donald has a hard ceiling
of 35% to 40%.

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:29.133
-There's a ceiling
beyond which he cannot go,

00:07:29.133 --> 00:07:32.000
and that ceiling
would not be 50%.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:35.200
-50% ceiling sounds like
a feature that real estate mogul

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.567
Donald Trump would try to sell

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:39.033
when you complain
about half the roof missing.

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:40.300
"You're complaining.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.434
You're complaining
about the rain

00:07:41.434 --> 00:07:42.634
pouring into your apartment.

00:07:42.634 --> 00:07:43.901
But let me tell you,
when it's sunny out,

00:07:43.901 --> 00:07:46.634
you're going to be thanking me
for this 50% deal.

00:07:46.634 --> 00:07:50.033
Everybody loves a 50% ceiling."

00:07:50.033 --> 00:07:51.634
Remember when everyone thought
Trump had a ceiling,

00:07:51.634 --> 00:07:53.400
even though he literally
started his campaign

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.868
at the top of an escalator?

00:07:54.868 --> 00:07:56.200
I mean, look at that guy.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.534
It's really hard to believe now

00:07:57.534 --> 00:07:59.934
he was headed to the most
powerful office in the world.

00:07:59.934 --> 00:08:01.934
He looks like he's headed
to Claire's

00:08:01.934 --> 00:08:03.033
to get his ears pierced.

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:04.901
[ Laughter ]

00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:07.667
"You guys go ahead.
I'll meet you at chess, gang."

00:08:09.734 --> 00:08:11.234
This is what keeps happening
with Trump.

00:08:11.234 --> 00:08:13.801
Republicans Just assume he's
done, that someone else

00:08:13.801 --> 00:08:15.434
will take him down,
but no one actually does it.

00:08:15.434 --> 00:08:16.834
And it's happening
all over again right now

00:08:16.834 --> 00:08:18.968
as Trump kicks off
his 2024 campaign.

00:08:18.968 --> 00:08:21.567
In a new article about the GOP's
refusal to take on

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:23.601
Trump directly,
one GOP consultant said...

00:08:26.701 --> 00:08:28.234
Another Republican,
who ran Marco Rubio's

00:08:28.234 --> 00:08:30.067
2016 campaign said...

00:08:39.834 --> 00:08:41.701
It doesn't even have to be
that heavy of a brick.

00:08:41.701 --> 00:08:43.934
If Donald Trump
were actually in the water,

00:08:43.934 --> 00:08:45.067
I'm pretty sure all I would take

00:08:45.067 --> 00:08:46.534
is to throw him a pebble
to sink him.

00:08:46.534 --> 00:08:49.067
You could throw him a pillow
even, though not a MyPillow.

00:08:49.067 --> 00:08:51.133
That thing is probably heavier.

00:08:51.133 --> 00:08:53.501
That's like 50 bricks.

00:08:53.501 --> 00:08:55.367
You try to sleep on one of
those, you immediately...

00:08:55.367 --> 00:08:56.467
-Wake up!

00:08:56.467 --> 00:08:58.267
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.267 --> 00:08:59.701
-And it's not just...

00:08:59.701 --> 00:09:03.400
[ Laughter ]

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.300
I mean, it should be
an alarm on your phone.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:08.067
I'm just saying.

00:09:08.067 --> 00:09:09.734
Just put it on Lindell
in the morning.

00:09:09.734 --> 00:09:13.000
You're gonna wake up.
It's not just Republicans.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.567
Even prosecutors are punting
when it comes to Trump.

00:09:15.567 --> 00:09:17.601
A new book has revealed
that days before Trump...

00:09:30.634 --> 00:09:31.868
...because Trump's
other scandals...

00:09:37.267 --> 00:09:39.601
They're all just waiting
for someone else to do it.

00:09:39.601 --> 00:09:41.701
It's like when you're at
a family party and Aunt Janet

00:09:41.701 --> 00:09:43.901
has one too many gin and tonics
and everyone knows

00:09:43.901 --> 00:09:45.834
and is just hoping
someone else will intervene

00:09:45.834 --> 00:09:47.100
and tell her
to put the glass down,

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.367
but then no one does it
and she ends up telling

00:09:48.367 --> 00:09:50.133
the entire family
about the exact time

00:09:50.133 --> 00:09:51.901
and location
your cousin was conceived.

00:09:51.901 --> 00:09:55.200
"Your Uncle Stu
wasn't exactly a romantic.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.534
We were at a Motel 6
in Niagara Falls,

00:09:57.534 --> 00:09:59.000
but they didn't have any rooms,

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.767
so we just went back
to the station wagon.

00:10:00.767 --> 00:10:03.167
And nine months later, boom!
Happy birthday, Kayleigh."

00:10:03.167 --> 00:10:05.367
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.033 --> 00:10:10.367
"Then I -- did I say a thing."

00:10:10.367 --> 00:10:12.834
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.834 --> 00:10:15.033
So that's how we got to
where we are now with Trump,

00:10:15.033 --> 00:10:17.534
a guy who fomented a coup
to overthrow American democracy,

00:10:17.534 --> 00:10:20.467
making official campaign stops
in early primary states.

00:10:20.467 --> 00:10:22.667
Even his prosecutors
and his fellow Republicans

00:10:22.667 --> 00:10:25.267
just sit on their hands waiting
for someone else to stop him.

00:10:25.267 --> 00:10:28.334
The parallels with 2016
are so eerie,

00:10:28.334 --> 00:10:31.200
we're even getting Trump doing
the same silly sound effects

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:32.534
he did
during his first campaign,

00:10:32.534 --> 00:10:34.267
like when he told this
random story in New Hampshire

00:10:34.267 --> 00:10:37.100
that I couldn't even follow him
about being on Air Force One.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.968
-So, we're landing.
We're getting 700.

00:10:38.968 --> 00:10:41.634
I say, "So, Captain."
I say, sure, it's fine.

00:10:41.634 --> 00:10:48.167
And so 600, 500, 400.

00:10:48.167 --> 00:10:49.334
Then he goes 300.

00:10:49.334 --> 00:10:52.567
So now we're 300 feet over,
which is nothing.

00:10:52.567 --> 00:10:55.100
And, "Captain,
we're okay, right?"

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:57.434
"Yes. Yes, sir."

00:10:57.434 --> 00:11:00.367
And then all of a sudden,
200, 100.

00:11:00.367 --> 00:11:03.133
I just close my eyes.

00:11:03.133 --> 00:11:06.467
Bing, bing, boom.
Landed it perfect.

00:11:06.467 --> 00:11:08.067
-Wait, that.

00:11:08.067 --> 00:11:11.167
[ Laughter ]

00:11:11.167 --> 00:11:12.667
That sounds so familiar.

00:11:12.667 --> 00:11:15.501
Oh, God, no.
No, it can't be happening again.

00:11:15.501 --> 00:11:17.968
-Bing, bing, bong, bong,
bing, bing, bing, bing.

00:11:17.968 --> 00:11:19.534
-Don't you see what's
happening?!

00:11:19.534 --> 00:11:22.467
Donald Trump has created
a time loop.

00:11:22.467 --> 00:11:24.501
We're all being
sucked back into.

00:11:24.501 --> 00:11:26.567
[ Echoing ] The year 2016.

00:11:26.567 --> 00:11:28.067
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:11:28.067 --> 00:11:29.267
[ Evil laughter ]

00:11:29.267 --> 00:11:31.467
-Bing, bing, bong, bong,
bing, bing, bing, bing.

00:11:31.467 --> 00:11:34.167
[ Laughter ]

00:11:34.167 --> 00:11:35.868
-2016.

00:11:35.868 --> 00:11:38.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:41.367 --> 00:11:43.200
They better not make me wear
a [bleep] suit again.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.934
[ Laughter ]

00:11:45.934 --> 00:11:48.801
Look at that.
Look at that beautiful baby boy.

00:11:48.801 --> 00:11:51.033
[ Laughter ]

00:11:51.033 --> 00:11:53.834
Trump is just up there as if he
never once incited a coup

00:11:53.834 --> 00:11:55.901
or oversaw one of the most
disastrous,

00:11:55.901 --> 00:11:57.834
chaotic presidencies
in American history.

00:11:57.834 --> 00:12:01.067
He's even freely taking shots
at his main rival, Ron DeSantis.

00:12:01.067 --> 00:12:02.634
No one in the GOP seems to care.

00:12:02.634 --> 00:12:05.267
In fact, Trump spent all weekend
going after DeSantis,

00:12:05.267 --> 00:12:06.801
calling him disloyal if he runs

00:12:06.801 --> 00:12:08.934
while he was
on his campaign plane

00:12:08.934 --> 00:12:10.501
flying from one stop
to the next.

00:12:10.501 --> 00:12:12.267
-So, Ron would have not be
governor

00:12:12.267 --> 00:12:14.901
if it wasn't for me,
and that's okay.

00:12:14.901 --> 00:12:18.300
And number one, he wouldn't have
gotten the nomination.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.801
And number two,
he wouldn't have beat

00:12:20.801 --> 00:12:23.100
his Democratic opponent.

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.434
So then when I hear
he might run, you know,

00:12:25.434 --> 00:12:26.901
I consider that very disloyal.

00:12:26.901 --> 00:12:29.334
But it's not about loyalty,
but to me it is.

00:12:29.334 --> 00:12:31.934
It's always about loyalty,
but for a lot of people.

00:12:31.934 --> 00:12:34.033
-Okay, first of all,
so psyched we're back to Trump

00:12:34.033 --> 00:12:35.434
doing press conferences
in places

00:12:35.434 --> 00:12:38.100
where we can barely hear him.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.100
You need to speak up, dude.

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.100
I can't believe I'm saying this,

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:41.467
but take a cue
from Mike Lindell.

00:12:41.467 --> 00:12:44.601
Also, do you think
Trump's insults are bad now?

00:12:44.601 --> 00:12:45.801
Wait until he sees
that picture

00:12:45.801 --> 00:12:49.167
of DeSantis in his fancy
white boots.

00:12:49.167 --> 00:12:50.968
It's a real picture.
Can you imagine what Trump

00:12:50.968 --> 00:12:53.968
is going to say once he sees
that picture of the DeSantis?

00:12:53.968 --> 00:12:55.167
"You know, it's not fair.

00:12:55.167 --> 00:12:56.734
Many people are sitting
around stole

00:12:56.734 --> 00:13:00.667
those fancy little boots from
the Dallas Cowboys cheerleaders.

00:13:00.667 --> 00:13:02.434
And he should give them back.
It's not nice.

00:13:02.434 --> 00:13:04.300
Those poor cheerleaders,
they have nothing to wear now.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.467
They have to cheerlead
in their bare feet, so sad."

00:13:06.467 --> 00:13:08.534
[ Laughter ]

00:13:08.534 --> 00:13:10.801
At so many turns
there was so many people

00:13:10.801 --> 00:13:12.801
who had the power to stop Trump
and make sure we didn't have

00:13:12.801 --> 00:13:14.601
to live through this nightmare
all over again.

00:13:14.601 --> 00:13:16.634
For one thing,
Republicans could have convicted

00:13:16.634 --> 00:13:17.767
him during his impeachment trial

00:13:17.767 --> 00:13:19.033
and disqualified him
from office.

00:13:19.033 --> 00:13:20.234
Instead, they're just
sitting on their hands,

00:13:20.234 --> 00:13:22.634
quietly hoping a magically
disappear strategy

00:13:22.634 --> 00:13:23.901
that failed in 2016.

00:13:23.901 --> 00:13:25.667
If Republicans don't take
on Trump directly,

00:13:25.667 --> 00:13:29.000
he could very well tear through
them like it did in 2016.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.067
And if he does,
it'll sound like this.

00:13:31.067 --> 00:13:33.601
-Bing, bing, bong, bong,
bing, bing, bing.

00:13:33.601 --> 00:13:35.467
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:35.467 --> 00:13:37.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

